      <div type="clause" n="48">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 48</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.9"/><pb n="519" ed="#liebermann"/>Nuls ne receit hom[e]<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.10"/> ultre III nuis, si [c]il<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.11"/> ne li<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.12"/> command<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="13" target="#LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.13"/>, od qui il fust ainz<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="14" target="#LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.14"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="519" ed="#liebermann"/>Ne quis hospitem ultra tres noctes non retineat. Nullus hospitem ultra terciam noctem recipiat, nisi ille cum quo prius fuit, hoc ei mandauerit.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="48" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="274" ed="#robertson"/>Nuls ne receit hom[e] ultre III nuis, si [c]il ne li command od qui il fust ainz.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="519" ed="#liebermann"/>48. Keiner nehme jemanden über drei Nächte lang auf<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_48.lnote.de1.b"/>, wenn ihm nicht dér [ihn] empfiehlt, bei dem derselbe bisher war.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">48. Let no one take someone in for longer than three nights unless he recommends [him] to him with whom the same was hitherto.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="275" ed="#robertson"/>No-one shall entertain a man for more than 3 days, unless he is committed to his charge by the man with whom he was formerly serving.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="519"><ref target="clause:IICn_28">II Cn 28</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 28</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 274–275 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 519, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">XLVI. <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">XLVI. I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hom <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hom I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">til <hi rend="italic">I</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">til I</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so</hi> (ihm), <hi rend="italic">nicht</hi> le (ihn)</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">so (to him), not le (him)</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.13" n="13" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">comand <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">comand Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_48.lnote.oe.14" n="14" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">amz <hi rend="italic">Im;</hi> aniz <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">amz Im; aniz Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="translationFootnote" xml:id="LeisWl_48.lnote.de1.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">519</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 30, 1</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">cf.</hi> 30, 1</seg></note>
      </div>
